---
title: Flatbread
time required: 90 minutes
servings: 6
image: https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhtIHy5ekgYY-rSYTA2wpzNNwAjoV8AXkBNSVcX6i0tWLmFY8QB8NvrBxu5qmqmwX38OT7ue0YvtyjezfA2ohB5Bn7amCS2aTeqkCeRuNzXHhLSUX1KJyukjwPQioINYbEyjSU5hQXbJtGU/s1600/Flatbread+%25289%2529.JPG
source: https://pamperedbeth.blogspot.com/2011/01/subway-flatbread-at-home-i-think-so.html?m=1
---

In #mixing bowl{}, sprinkle @active dry yeast{1%Tbsp} over @water{1%cup}(warm, around 100°F). Add @sugar{1/4%cup}, give a light stir, and let sit until frothy. 

Beat @egg{1} and add to yeast water along with @milk{3%Tbsp} and @salt{1%tsp}. 

Stir in @flour{1.5%cup} until mixture is creamy.

Add more @flour{1.5%cup}, and then continue to add @?flour{2%cup} as needed until a soft dough forms. 

Knead for ~{6-8%minutes}. 

In warm place, let dough rise until doubled ~{45-60%minutes}. 

Punch down and divide into 6-12 balls, depending on desired size of bread. 

> 6 balls should do about 6-inch x 6-inch pieces (maybe bigger) - perfect for sandwiches like Subway. Twelve would do about 12 3-inch rounds - this would be good if you are just serving the flat bread with soup. 

Let dough rest for ~{15%minutes}.

Melt @butter{1/2%cup} and add @?onion powder{} and @?garlic salt{} to taste. 

Heat #grill pan{} over high heat. 

Punch down then roll out 1 of the rolls of dough. Roll it to about 1/4 inch thick. 

> These will expand a little while cooking so make sure they aren't TOO thick. If they are too thin they will come out more like cracker bread. 

Turn the heat down to LOW for the grill pan. 

Brush butter over rolled out dough. Lay it face down in the grill pan and cook (for me, it took about 2-3 minutes on low-2 setting). If desired, butter the uncooked side and flip over.

Repeat for remaining dough.